        "original_id": "5c3a0b66-9e3b-52f5-adae-742afad5fce3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Pinocchio (1940 film), Home on the Range (2004 film)\n- Song: \"I've Got No Strings\"\n- People: Carlo Collodi, Dickie Jones, Chris Sauve\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, Walt Disney Feature Animation, Walt Disney Pictures\n- TV Shows: The Raccoons, The Ren and Stimpy Show, Futurama, Baby Blues\n\nFacts:\n- Pinocchio is a 1940 American animated musical fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Productions and based on Carlo Collodi's Italian children's novel The Adventures of Pinocchio.\n- Pinocchio was the second animated feature film produced by Disney, after the success of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs in 1937.\n- \"I've Got No Strings,\" also known as \"I Got No Strings,\" is a song from Disney's animated film Pinocchio sung by Dickie Jones as Pinocchio.\n- Home on the Range is a 2004 American animated musical western comedy film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation and released by Walt Disney Pictures.\n- Chris Sauve has worked on the television shows The Raccoons, The Ren and Stimpy Show, Futurama, and Baby Blues.\n- Chris Sauve has also worked on the films The Iron Giant and Home on the Range.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c2bb131d-00a1-5fcd-9c5e-79729386e5ac",
        "text": "Page: Pinocchio (1940 film). Sentence: Pinocchio is a 1940 American animated musical fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Productions and based on the Italian children's novel \"The Adventures of Pinocchio\" by Carlo Collodi.\nPage: Pinocchio (1940 film). Sentence: It was the second animated feature film produced by Disney, made after the success of \"Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs\" (1937).\nPage: Home on the Range (2004 film). Sentence: Home on the Range is a 2004 American animated musical western comedy film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation and released by Walt Disney Pictures.\nPage: I've Got No Strings. Sentence: \"I've Got No Strings\" also known as \"I Got No Strings\" is a song from Walt Disney's animated film \"Pinocchio\" sung by Dickie Jones as Pinocchio.\nPage: Chris Sauve. Sentence: He has worked on several television shows (\"The Raccoons, The Ren and Stimpy Show\", \"Futurama\", \"Baby Blues\") and films (\"Iron Giant\", \"Home on the Range\").",
